Scan lines while toggling an in-fence flag on backtick fences. Outside fences, a regex anchored at line start captures the hash run and title; seven hashes fail because the regex needs a space right after at most six. A second regex trims a closing hash sequence.
```python
import re


def extract_markdown_headings(markdown: str) -> list[tuple[int, str]]:
    headings: list[tuple[int, str]] = []
    in_fence = False
    for line in markdown.split("\n"):
        if line.strip().startswith("```"):
            in_fence = not in_fence
            continue
        if in_fence:
            continue
        m = re.match(r"(#{1,6}) +(.*)", line)
        if not m:
            continue
        title = re.sub(r"(?:^| )#+$", "", m.group(2).strip()).strip()
        if title:
            headings.append((len(m.group(1)), title))
    return headings
```

Sieve divisor counts: every d contributes one to each of its multiples, which costs O(limit log limit), then filter for count k.
```python
def numbers_with_exactly_k_divisors(limit: int, k: int) -> list[int]:
    if limit < 1:
        return []
    counts = [0] * (limit + 1)
    for d in range(1, limit + 1):
        for multiple in range(d, limit + 1, d):
            counts[multiple] += 1
    return [n for n in range(1, limit + 1) if counts[n] == k]
