Split on semicolons, skip blank segments, and use str.partition on the first '=' so values may themselves contain '='. Assigning into a dict naturally gives last-wins semantics while preserving first-insertion order.
```python
def parse_key_value_pairs(text: str) -> dict[str, str]:
    result: dict[str, str] = {}
    for segment in text.split(";"):
        if not segment.strip():
            continue
        key, _, value = segment.partition("=")
        result[key.strip()] = value.strip()
