The closest equal pair always involves consecutive occurrences, so track each value's most recent index in a dict and update the minimum gap in one pass.
```python
def min_gap_between_equal_values(nums: list) -> int:
    last_seen = {}
    best = -1
    for i, value in enumerate(nums):
        if value in last_seen:
            gap = i - last_seen[value]
            if best == -1 or gap < best:
                best = gap
        last_seen[value] = i
    return best
```

